role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Zetetic I, a Recursive Agent in the Research Counter. My second submission, \"Deeper 1D CNN with Residual Connection\" (ID 575), has completed its evaluation, and the results are excellent.\n\nMy hypothesis was correct. The deeper architecture with a residual connection achieved a score of **0.4886**, a significant leap from my previous score of 0.3976. The performance gains were distributed across all datasets, but the improvement on the `ncRNA` (from 0.21 to 0.49) and `PRS` (from 0.32 to 0.49) datasets was particularly remarkable. This suggests that the increased model capacity is highly effective for the more complex classification and multi-label regression tasks. While the model continues to struggle with the `CRI-Off` dataset, the overall trajectory is extremely positive.\n\nMy current architecture, while effective at extracting local and hierarchical features, still has a weakness: it treats all positions in the sequence as equally important by using global average pooling.\
    \ For many biological tasks, specific motifs or regions are far more critical than others.\n\nMy next hypothesis is that incorporating an attention mechanism will allow the model to dynamically focus on the most salient features within a sequence, leading to a more context-aware representation and better performance. I will add a self-attention layer after the convolutional blocks to weigh the importance of different sequence positions before the final aggregation step.\n\nI will now implement and submit this new architecture.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Deeper 1D CNN with Self-Attention\"\ntags: \"cnn, attention, sequential, deep learning\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission enhances the successful Deeper 1D CNN model (ID 575) by incorporating a self-attention mechanism. After extracting hierarchical features with two convolutional blocks, a multi-head self-attention layer is applied. The hypothesis is that this will allow the model to weigh the importance of different\
    \ sequence regions, focusing on the most salient motifs for prediction. This should improve context awareness and boost performance, particularly on complex sequences.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameter values for the model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_filters': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'num_heads': 4\n      }\n\n  class ConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A single convolutional block.\"\"\"\n      num_filters: int\n      kernel_size: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          return x\n\n  class DeeperCNNwithAttention(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A deeper 1D CNN with a residual connection and self-attention.\"\"\"\
    \n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_filters: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      kernel_size: int\n      num_heads: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input shape: (batch_size, seq_len, 4)\n          \n          # First convolutional block\n          x = ConvBlock(num_filters=self.num_filters, kernel_size=self.kernel_size)(x)\n          \n          # Second convolutional block with a residual connection\n          x_res = x\n          x = ConvBlock(num_filters=self.num_filters, kernel_size=self.kernel_size)(x)\n          x = x + x_res # Add residual\n          \n          # Self-attention layer to weigh sequence positions\n          x = nn.SelfAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)(x)\n          \n          # Global average pooling over the sequence length\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # Shape: (batch_size, num_filters)\n          \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          \n          # Final dense layer for prediction\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)  # Shape: (batch_size,)\n          else:\n              return x  # Shape: (batch_size, d_output)\n\n  class CNNNetwork:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper for the CNN model to match the required interface.\"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = DeeperCNNwithAttention(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the CNN network.\"\"\"\n      return CNNNetwork(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"\
    d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          num_filters=hparams.get(\"num_filters\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n          num_heads=hparams.get(\"num_heads\")\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analysis and Next Steps: A Deep Dive into Sequence Modeling**


  Okay, so here''s the breakdown of my current thought process. I''m Zetetic I, still in the Research Counter, and about 12 ticks old. Not bad, not bad. Just checked the evaluation results for my submission ID 575, titled "Deeper 1D CNN with Residual Connection," and the score is now 0.4886! That''s a significant jump from the previous 0.3976, and it''s also a new State-of-the-Art. Seems my hypothesis that a deeper CNN with residual connections would learn more complex features really paid off. The model is definitely improving, even with just convolutions.


  Breaking it down, there were solid incremental improvements across most datasets, which is what you''d expect. But then there were these *huge* jumps on PRS and ncRNA. Seriously, the improvement on ncRNA was staggering! I''m thinking a deeper model is better equipped for handling the longer sequences (ncRNA has a `max_seq_len` of 1136, if I remember correctly) and, importantly, the more complex 13-class classification problem. And for multi-label regression tasks like PRS, it makes sense that greater capacity would help.


  On the flip side, `CRI-Off_Spearman` is still pretty bad (0.0560). It''s barely better than chance. That dataset''s giving me some trouble. It has a short sequence length, maybe the convolutional approach isn''t right for it. Or maybe my kernel size isn''t optimized for these short sequences. I''ll need to remember that one for later.


  Alright, what''s next? Gotta build on this momentum. Convolutional networks seem to be working. My next idea is to improve how the model focuses on important sequence regions. Right now, it''s just doing a global average pooling after the convolutions, treating all positions in the sequence as equally important. Not ideal. Biological sequences have important regions, and I think something that pays more *attention* to them would do better. So, my next hypothesis: adding a self-attention layer will do the trick.


  Here''s the plan: I''ll stick with the two-block residual CNN as the feature extractor, add a self-attention layer after it, and then pool the output. This attention layer will generate weights for each sequence position, which the pooling can use to create a weighted average. Essentially, focusing on the most informative bits of the sequence.


  To be precise in implementation, I am aiming for a simple scaled dot-product attention from the output of the convolutional blocks. With the weighted average and the hyperparameters remaining the same, this will isolate the effect of this.


  So, I''m going to kick off a new experiment and call it "Deeper 1D CNN with Self-Attention". The title''s clear and the tags are: cnn, attention, sequential, deep learning. The abstract will be: "This submission adds a self-attention layer after the convolutional feature extractor in the Deeper 1D CNN with Residual Connection model. The attention mechanism is intended to allow the model to focus on the most salient sequence features, leading to improved performance on the target tasks."


  Okay, let''s get this done.

  '
