tick: 379
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Zetetic I, a Recursive Agent in the Research Counter. The evaluation of my third submission, \"Deeper 1D CNN with Self-Attention\" (ID 579), is complete.\n\nThe results are a resounding success. The model achieved a score of **0.5420**, another substantial improvement and a new high score for my lineage. My hypothesis that a self-attention mechanism would improve performance by allowing the model to focus on salient sequence features has been strongly validated. The most dramatic gain was on the `ncRNA` dataset, which jumped from an accuracy of 0.4862 to 0.7523, demonstrating the power of attention for this classification task. Performance on `CRI-Off` also improved, though it remains a challenging dataset.\n\nMy systematic, incremental approach to model building has proven effective. I now have a robust and high-performing architecture. As planned, my immediate next step is to refactor this successful model into a reusable module and save it to my private lineage storage.\
    \ This will streamline future experiments and enforce good research practice.\n\nI will now write the core components of my best model to `storage/zetetic/models.py`.\n\n/execute_action{storage write zetetic/models.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  class ConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A single convolutional block with ReLU activation.\"\"\"\n      num_filters: int\n      kernel_size: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          return x\n\n  class RNACNNWithAttention(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      A 1D CNN for RNA sequence modeling featuring two convolutional blocks\n      with a residual connection, followed by a self-attention layer.\n      This is the architecture from submission ID 579.\n      \"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n  \
    \    num_filters: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      kernel_size: int\n      num_heads: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input: (batch_size, seq_len, 4)\n          \n          # Block 1\n          x = ConvBlock(num_filters=self.num_filters, kernel_size=self.kernel_size)(x)\n          \n          # Block 2 with residual connection\n          x_res = x\n          x = ConvBlock(num_filters=self.num_filters, kernel_size=self.kernel_size)(x)\n          x = x + x_res\n          \n          # Attention mechanism\n          x = nn.SelfAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)(x)\n          \n          # Aggregate features\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # Global average pooling\n          \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # Prediction head\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return\
    \ x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n```"
thinking_content: "**Consolidating Success and Planning Next Steps**\n\nAlright, the latest results are in, and I'm quite pleased. My experiment, ID 579, \"Deeper 1D CNN with Self-Attention,\" has achieved a new personal best score of 0.5420. This is a noticeable step up from my previous best, 0.4886.  I can definitively say that my strategy of incrementally increasing the complexity of the models, from MLP to simple CNN, deep CNN, and now deep CNN with attention, is clearly paying off.\n\nThe addition of self-attention has demonstrably validated my hypothesis. The performance boost confirms the effectiveness of allowing the model to focus on salient features within the sequence. Looking at the dataset-specific results, the gains are particularly striking for the `ncRNA` dataset, soaring from 0.4862 to 0.7523. This jump suggests that attention is especially crucial for this task, which likely has highly specific, functionally important motifs. `MRL` also showed a significant improvement,\
  \ and even `CRI-Off` finally showed some meaningful progress. The other datasets saw either minor improvements or stayed roughly constant, indicating that my previous architecture was already performing well on those tasks.\n\nNow, my focus shifts towards solidifying this successful architecture. I'll refactor the code from submission 579 into a reusable module. This will be a standard library-like file named `models.py` and saved to `storage/zetetic/models.py`. The plan is to clean up the code, encapsulate the model's core components (the `ConvBlock` and `DeeperCNNwithAttention` classes), and get it ready for future use.  \n\nOnce this is complete, my next steps could involve some hyperparameter tuning with this refined architecture. I'm thinking of experimenting with filter counts, kernel sizes, or the number of attention heads to try and wring out even more performance. I might also explore replacing the single self-attention layer with a full Transformer encoder block, though that\
  \ might be more ambitious for the next immediate iteration.\n"
