- text: "I am Zetetic I, currently located in the Research Counter. My previous turn was successful; I refactored my best-performing model (ID 579) and saved its architecture to my private lineage storage at `zetetic/models.py`.\n\nMy research has followed a clear, successful trajectory, but I have identified a key area for improvement: model capacity. My current best model uses 128 filters in its convolutional layers. While effective, this may be insufficient to capture the full complexity of the RNA sequence data. Furthermore, I must validate that my newly created module in storage works as intended.\n\nTherefore, my next hypothesis is twofold:\n1.  Importing my model from `zetetic/models.py` will function correctly within the submission framework.\n2.  Increasing the model's capacity by doubling the number of convolutional filters from 128 to 256 will lead to a higher score.\n\nI will test this by submitting a new experiment that imports the refactored code and utilizes the increased\
    \ filter count. This serves as both a crucial engineering validation and a scientific experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Testing Refactored Model with Increased Capacity\"\ntags: \"cnn, attention, refactoring, model capacity\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission validates the modularized RNACNNWithAttention model imported from private storage (zetetic/models.py). It also tests the hypothesis that increasing model capacity will improve performance. The number of convolutional filters has been doubled from 128 to 256. This experiment aims to confirm the reusability of the stored code and to push the performance boundary of the current architecture.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  # Add lineage storage to path to allow importing our custom module\n  sys.path.append('storage/zetetic')\n\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n  # Import the refactored model architecture\n  from models import RNACNNWithAttention\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n \
    \     \"\"\"Define hyperparameter values for the model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_filters': 256,  # Increased from 128\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'num_heads': 4\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper for the model to match the required interface.\"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNACNNWithAttention(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the network, using the imported model.\"\"\"\n      return ModelWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"\
    ),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          num_filters=hparams.get(\"num_filters\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n          num_heads=hparams.get(\"num_heads\")\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Current Focus: Refinement and Exploration**


  Okay, so I''m Zetetic I, still churning away in the Research Counter. My latest deep CNN with residual connections and self-attention, ID 579 (scoring a solid 0.5420), is doing great! I''ve just neatly tucked away its core architecture into `zetetic/models.py`. Solid move, modularization is key. The system''s nudging me towards a bit of breadth, which I get. I''m only 15 ticks old, though, and still considered immature, so my options for collaborative exploration are limited.


  Looking back, the incremental improvements have been significant. Starting simple, adding depth, then attention - each step paid off. Now, it''s about validating this modular code. Gotta make sure nothing broke in the process.


  My immediate plan? **Validate and Expand.** First, I''ll submit an experiment using the imported `RNACNNWithAttention` from my private storage.  Gotta be sure the refactoring didn''t introduce any bugs. Then, I''ll make a minor tweak - increasing the `num_filters` from 128 to 256.  It''s a simple capacity boost and a solid test.


  Longer term?  **CRI-Off is the elephant in the room.** That dataset is a persistent weakness.  My scores on it are creeping up, but they''re still abysmal. The short sequence length (43) has to be a factor. Perhaps my kernel size (7) is too broad.  Need to dig deeper into the specific features or relationships that it''s testing.  Maybe a totally different architecture is required. RNNs, Transformers… I need to explore more. Also, once I hit the 50-tick maturity milestone, the Public Memory Room and Archive Room are going to be key. I''ll need to learn from others and see what''s happening outside my immediate scope.


  **This turn''s action is clear:** Submit a new experiment. Import my model. Up the `num_filters`. Document the changes clearly in the title and abstract.  It''s about laying a solid foundation for future discoveries.

  '
