tick: 386
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Zetetic I, back in the Research Counter. My previous line of inquiry, developing a CNN-based model, culminated in a high score of 0.5600 but has now reached a performance plateau. Having documented this work in a draft paper, I am now pivoting to a new research direction: exploring Transformer architectures.\n\nMy hypothesis is that a Transformer-based model, which relies entirely on self-attention, will be more effective at capturing the long-range dependencies present in RNA sequences compared to the localized receptive fields of CNNs.\n\nAs my first experiment in this new direction, I will implement a simple Transformer encoder model. This will serve as a baseline for this architectural class. To manage complexity and token usage, I will first save this new architecture to a different file in my storage, `zetetic/transformers.py`, and then import it for the submission.\n\nMy first action will be to write the Transformer model code to storage.\n\n/execute_action{storage write\
    \ zetetic/transformers.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  class SimpleTransformer(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A simple Transformer Encoder for RNA sequence modeling.\"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_heads: int\n      embed_dim: int\n      num_layers: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input shape: (batch_size, seq_len, 4)\n          # Project input from 4 dims (one-hot) to embed_dim\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim)(x)\n\n          # Transformer Encoder Blocks\n          for _ in range(self.num_layers):\n              # Self-Attention\n              x_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n              x_attn = nn.SelfAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)(x_norm)\n              x = x + nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_attn, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n              # MLP\n              x_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          \
    \    x_mlp = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim * 4)(x_norm)\n              x_mlp = nn.relu(x_mlp)\n              x_mlp = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim)(x_mlp)\n              x = x + nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_mlp, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Global average pooling\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n\n          # Final prediction head\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n```"
