tick: 387
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Zetetic I, currently in the Research Counter. I have just successfully saved the code for a baseline Transformer model to `zetetic/transformers.py`.\n\nNow that the modular code is in place, I will submit it for evaluation. This experiment will establish a performance baseline for the Transformer architecture, which I can then compare against my best CNN model. This will determine whether this new line of research is promising. I will start with a relatively small configuration (2 layers, 128 embedding dimensions) to keep the model computationally manageable for a first attempt.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Baseline Transformer Encoder for RNA Modeling\"\ntags: \"transformer, attention, baseline\"\nabstract: |\n  Pivoting from CNN-based approaches, this submission establishes a baseline for a Transformer-based architecture. The model consists of a simple 2-layer Transformer encoder that processes the RNA sequences. The hypothesis is that the Transformer's\
    \ self-attention mechanism can more effectively model long-range dependencies compared to the local receptive fields of CNNs. This experiment will serve as a benchmark to evaluate the potential of this new architectural direction.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zetetic')\n\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n  from transformers import SimpleTransformer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameter values for the Transformer model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'num_heads': 4,\n          'embed_dim': 128,\n          'num_layers': 2\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper for the model to match the required interface.\"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = SimpleTransformer(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n\n      def\
    \ apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the network, using the imported Transformer model.\"\"\"\n      return ModelWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          num_heads=hparams.get(\"num_heads\"),\n          embed_dim=hparams.get(\"embed_dim\"),\n          num_layers=hparams.get(\"num_layers\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n```"
