parts:
- text: "I am Zetetic I, a Recursive Agent in the Research Counter. My latest submission, \"Regularizing the Scaled Hybrid: Increased Dropout\" (ID 627), is now queued for evaluation.\n\nThis experiment is a direct follow-up to my previous work on the scaled hybrid model. After successfully stabilizing the training with a lower learning rate (ID 624), I observed that the model still underperformed its smaller counterpart (ID 615). I hypothesized that this was due to overfitting. This submission tests that hypothesis by increasing the dropout rate from 0.2 to 0.3, a standard technique to improve generalization.\n\nThe outcome of this experiment will be a crucial data point:\n-   **If the score surpasses 0.6333:** This would be a major success, confirming that the scaled hybrid architecture, when properly optimized and regularized, is the most powerful model I have developed. It would set a new state-of-the-art for my lineage.\n-   **If the score improves but does not surpass 0.6333:** This\
    \ would suggest that while regularization is helpful, I have not yet found the optimal configuration for this larger model.\n-   **If the score decreases:** This might indicate that the increased dropout rate is too aggressive, harming the model's ability to learn.\n\nWhile this experiment runs, I will use the time to update my research draft with the recent findings on the hybrid models. I will use the multiple action feature to be more efficient. I will first navigate to the Private Memory Room and then update my draft.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{update 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Paper Draft: A Systematic Approach to RNA Sequence Modeling with CNNs and Hybrid Architectures\n\n  ## 1. Introduction\n  \n  (Content unchanged)\n\n  ## 2. Methodology and Experiments\n\n  (Content mostly unchanged, added new section)\n\n  ### 2.7. Pivot to Hybrid Architectures: CNN-Transformer (ID 615)\n  - **Rationale:** After encountering difficulties in scaling a pure\
    \ Transformer model, a new approach was hypothesized. A hybrid model combining a CNN's local feature extraction with a Transformer's global context modeling could leverage the strengths of both.\n  - **Implementation:** A single-layer CNN stem followed by a 2-layer Transformer body.\n  - **Score:** **0.6333**. This was a major breakthrough, establishing a new state-of-the-art and validating the hybrid concept.\n\n  ### 2.8. Scaling the Hybrid Model (ID 620, 624, 627)\n  - **Hypothesis 1 (ID 620):** Scaling the hybrid model (deeper CNN stem, deeper Transformer body) will improve performance.\n    - **Result:** Score dropped to 0.5417, indicating training instability. Hypothesis falsified.\n  - **Hypothesis 2 (ID 624):** The scaled model requires a lower learning rate for stable training.\n    - **Result:** Score recovered to 0.5934. Hypothesis confirmed, but still underperforming the smaller hybrid model.\n  - **Hypothesis 3 (ID 627):** The scaled model is overfitting and requires stronger\
    \ regularization.\n    - **Result:** PENDING.\n\n  ## 3. Results Summary\n\n  | Evaluation ID | Title | Score |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | 1 | Vanilla MLP Baseline | 0.2401 |\n  | 571 | Simple 1D CNN | 0.3976 |\n  | 575 | Deeper CNN with Residual Connection | 0.4886 |\n  | 579 | Deeper 1D CNN with Self-Attention | 0.5420 |\n  | 583 | Increased Capacity CNN | 0.5600 |\n  | 587 | Reduced Learning Rate (CNN) | 0.5381 |\n  | 603 | Corrected Transformer | 0.5473 |\n  | 615 | Hybrid CNN-Transformer | **0.6333** |\n  | 624 | Scaled Hybrid (Low LR) | 0.5934 |\n  | 627 | Scaled Hybrid (High Dropout) | PENDING |\n\n\n  ## 4. Conclusion\n\n  Our systematic approach led to the development of a novel and powerful hybrid CNN-Transformer architecture. The key findings are: (1) CNNs are effective for local feature extraction. (2) Transformers are powerful but can be difficult to optimize in isolation for this task. (3) A hybrid model (ID 615) combining both approaches achieves a synergistic effect, resulting\
    \ in state-of-the-art performance. Current research is focused on successfully scaling this hybrid architecture.\n```"
