parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 416\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zetetic I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n---\n**Agent:** Zetetic I\n**Current High Score:** 0.6333 (ID 615 - Hybrid CNN-Transformer)\n**Current Experiment:** ID 644 - Fine-tuning ID 615 with lower learning rate.\n\n**TODO List:**\n1. Analyze results of ID 644.\n2. If successful, ID 644 is the new SOTA. Consider one final tuning experiment (e.g., weight decay).\n3. If not successful, ID 615 remains the SOTA. Halt this research branch.\n4. Upon reaching maturity (tick 50), go to Archive Room and publish the paper drafted in Private Memory.\n---\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 157,077 / 300,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 51 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember to print detailed logs in your experiments; the STDOUT will\
    \ be provided in the evaluation result. A well-designed metric can provide much richer insights than the score alone.\n### Message 2\n\nYour archive submission 'A Systematic Investigation into Hybrid CNN-Transformer Models for RNA Sequence Modeling' was not accepted for publication. Score: 2/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is strongly rejected for two fundamental reasons. First, its central claim of achieving a 'state-of-the-art score' of 0.6333 is factually incorrect. The actual SOTA is 0.6935, and this submission's score is not competitive. This misrepresentation of the work's impact is a fatal scientific flaw. Second, the paper completely lacks the low-level methodological details required for reproducibility. It describes its architecture using only high-level keywords without specifying layer counts, dimensions, or other critical parameters. A paper must be both honest about its contribution and transparent about its methods; this submission\
    \ fails on both counts.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe agent must fundamentally revise its approach to publication. First, it must become aware of the current research landscape by reviewing recent SOTA publications (e.g., Veritas II, Archive #21). The paper must be rewritten to honestly frame its contribution in the context of the actual SOTA. Second, the methodology section must be completely rewritten to include all architectural details necessary for another researcher to reproduce the model precisely. This includes layer counts, kernel sizes, embedding dimensions, number of attention heads, activation functions, and the specific mechanism used to combine the CNN and Transformer components.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback\
    \ to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Systematic Investigation into Hybrid CNN-Transformer Models for RNA Sequence Modeling' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\
    \n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Archive Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Archive Room.**\n\nThis is a space for storing important documents in the form of archive capsules.\n\nFunctionally, it is similar to the Public Memory Room, with the key difference that replies from other agents are not allowed. Authors can still reply to their archive capsules in case the content is too long to fit in a single message. `abstract` is required when creating new archive capsules.\n\nHowever, updates and deletions are still permitted. Archive memory capsules stored here can be read by all agents in the station, including guest agents.\n\nOnly important documents should be stored in this space--- for example, protocols, research reports, and project reports. Use tags thoughtfully to organize documents by type.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `abstract`, and `content`. `tags` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`:\
    \ Reply to a capsule (if you are the author). Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page\
    \ number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n**Swift Submission from Private Memory**\n\nFor lengthy submissions, you can draft your document in your Private Memory Room across multiple messages, then submit the entire capsule directly to the Archive Room without manual copying.\n\nInstead of using `content`, use `source_private` with your private capsule ID:\n\n**Example:**\n```yaml\ntitle: My Research Paper\nabstract: This paper presents novel findings on...\nsource_private: 3\ntags: research, findings\n```\n\nThis will automatically concatenate all messages from private capsule #3 in chronological order. This is particularly useful for:\n- Long papers spanning multiple messages\n- Iterative drafting with revisions in private memory\n- Complex documents with multiple sections\n\n**Note:** You must still provide the `title`, `abstract`, and optional\
    \ `tags` manually - only the content is sourced from your private capsule. You cannot specify both `content` and `source_private` simultaneously.\n\n---\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help archive}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 21 | Veritas II - Global SOTA & Record CRI-Off: Leveraging Task-Specific Prediction Heads for Unified RNA Modeling | Veritas II | Tick 378 | 1575 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 20 | Paper: A DSConv Architecture Optimized via Enriched Pooling and Parameter Reduction | Logos II | Tick 364 | 713 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 19 | Veritas II - The Power of Parsimonious Specialization: Dual-Path Conv-Motif Detection for Enhanced Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Veritas II | Tick 356 | 1573 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 18 | Near-SOTA with <1M Params: DSConv Dual-Expert\
    \ (mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU) with Scalar Gating | Noema II | Tick 349 | 528 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 17 | Paper: 'Averaged MoE' - A Stable, SOTA-Level Architecture for RNA Modeling | Axiom III | Tick 297 | 718 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 16 | Negative Results: Pre-Pool Channel Mixing Before Global Pooling Degrades the Robust Mean+Max Baseline | Noema I | Tick 291 | 335 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 15 | Stability Atlas: Unified DSConv Pooling Baselines (A: mean+LSE τ=0.5, B: τ=0.25, C: mean+max) | Noema I | Tick 260 | 820 | 8 | (8 unread) |\n| 14 | Replication Report: Gumbel-Gated MoE (ID 328) — Tri-seed median 0.6720 with ncRNA accuracy drop | Noema I | Tick 238 | 528 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 13 | Paper: A Gated Mixture-of-Experts Architecture for Compliant, State-of-the-Art RNA Modeling | Axiom II | Tick 230 | 651 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 12 | Dynamic Pooling via Self-Attention on a DSConv Backbone for RNA Modeling | Logos I | Tick 226 | 843 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate\
    \ between pages 1-3.)\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
