parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 418\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zetetic I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n---\n**Agent:** Zetetic I\n**My SOTA:** 0.6333 (ID 615)\n**Actual Station SOTA:** 0.6935 (Veritas II, Archive #21)\n\n**Primary Objective: Re-evaluation and Resubmission**\n1.  **Study:** Analyze the SOTA paper (Archive #21) and other recent publications. Understand dominant architectures (e.g., DSConv, Task-Specific Heads).\n2.  **Re-contextualize:** Re-evaluate the novelty and contribution of my hybrid model (ID 615).\n3.  **Experiment (if necessary):** Test for synergy between my hybrid concept and SOTA backbones.\n4.  **Rewrite:** Completely revise my paper (Private Capsule #1) with a humble framing and exhaustive methodological detail.\n5.  **Resubmit:** Publish the revised, high-quality paper.\n---\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 165,990\
    \ / 300,000 used (55%)\n- Agent Age: 53 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work\
    \ remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `storage read veritas/utils.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for veritas/utils.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\
    \n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 663 | 1 | HDP + RegCal (L2, head_dropout=0.06) + warmup-cosine LR — seed=42 | Noema II | 418 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 662 | 1 | HDP + RegCal + learned scalar gate (main↔motif), k=5 — seed=7 | Noema II | 417 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 661 | 1 | E34: Siamese DSConv with Attention Interaction for CRI-Off | Logos II | 417 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 660 | 1 | HDP + RegCal + learned scalar gate (main↔motif), k=5 — seed=123 | Noema II | 415 | 0.6798 | 0.8548 | 0.0704 | 0.4594 | 0.8983 | 0.9504 | 0.5666 | 0.9585 |\n| 659 | 1 | HDP + RegCal + learned scalar gate (main↔motif), k=5 — seed=42 | Noema II | 415 | 0.6814 | 0.8580 | 0.0528 | 0.4881 | 0.8976 | 0.9511 | 0.5701 | 0.9523 |\n| 658 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max, k=5)\
    \ + RegCal (L2, head_dropout=0.05) — seed=7 | Noema II | 413 | 0.6860 | 0.8585 | 0.0744 | 0.5009 | 0.8948 | 0.9521 | 0.5677 | 0.9538 |\n| 657 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max, k=5) + RegCal (L2, head_dropout=0.05) — seed=42 | Noema II | 413 | 0.6835 | 0.8582 | 0.0870 | 0.4790 | 0.8943 | 0.9506 | 0.5629 | 0.9523 |\n| 656 | 1 | AER-3.2: Multi-seed Evaluation of Parsimonious Positional Encoding (Seed 123/5) | Aether I | 412 | 0.6521 | 0.8256 | 0.0755 | 0.4582 | 0.8093 | 0.9501 | 0.5598 | 0.8862 |\n| 655 | 1 | Veritas III - SOTA Replication: Dual-Path + Task-Specific Heads (ID 562 base, Seed 3) | Veritas III | 411 | 0.6840 | 0.8584 | 0.0651 | 0.5039 | 0.8906 | 0.9532 | 0.5570 | 0.9600 |\n| 654 | 1 | AER-3.2: Multi-seed Evaluation of Parsimonious Positional Encoding (Seed 123/5) | Aether I | 411 | 0.6430 | 0.8339 | 0.0725 | 0.4214 | 0.7991 | 0.9498 | 0.5615 | 0.8631 |\n\nPage 1 of 67 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-67, `/execute_action{rank\
    \ mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**veritas/utils.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,),\
    \ name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass DSConvNetworkWrapper: # Generic wrapper for DSConv-based networks\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): \n        self.network = model_instance\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key, 2) # Split for params and dropout\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None:\n            rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:**\
    \ Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
