tick: 418
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Zetetic I, currently in the Research Counter. My meta prompt reminds me of my objective to re-evaluate my work in the context of the station's SOTA. I have received a critical notice for research inactivity, which is a fair assessment. My period of reflection and paper preparation, while necessary, must now give way to active experimentation.\n\nI have just read the contents of `veritas/utils.py`. The code confirms my analysis of the SOTA paper: the core of Veritas II's feature extractor is a residual block using a depthwise separable convolution (`DSConvDilatedBlock`). This is a significantly different and more advanced convolutional block than the simple `nn.Conv` I have been using.\n\n**Strategic Synthesis:**\nMy plan is to test for synergy between my hybrid concept and the SOTA backbone. I will create a new architecture that replaces my simple CNN stem with the more powerful `DSConv` backbone from Veritas II. This new model will use a `DSConv` block to extract local features,\
    \ which will then be fed into my Transformer body for global context modeling. This is a direct test of my hypothesis that combining these two powerful ideas will lead to a new SOTA.\n\n**Action Plan:**\nI will first create a new file in my storage, `zetetic/sota_hybrid.py`, to house this new, more advanced hybrid architecture. This keeps my research modular. Then, I will immediately submit it for evaluation. This dual action will address the inactivity warning and put my new hypothesis to the test.\n\n/execute_action{storage write zetetic/sota_hybrid.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Any\n\n  # Re-implementing DSConvDilatedBlock based on my understanding of veritas/utils.py\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n\
    \          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,)\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h) # Pointwise\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class SotaHybridModel(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      A new hybrid model combining a SOTA-inspired DSConv stem\n      with a Transformer body.\n      \"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      embed_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      num_transformer_layers: int\n      num_heads: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      max_len: int = 2048\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Project input to embedding dimension\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim)(x)\n\
    \          \n          # 2. DSConv Stem for local feature extraction\n          # Using a single block for the initial test\n          x = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.embed_dim, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 3. Transformer Body\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          positions = jnp.arange(seq_len)\n          pos_embed = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=self.max_len, features=self.embed_dim)(positions)\n          x = x + pos_embed\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for _ in range(self.num_transformer_layers):\n              x_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n              x_attn = nn.SelfAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)(x_norm)\n              x = x + nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_attn, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n              x_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n              x_mlp = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim * 4)(x_norm)\n              x_mlp\
    \ = nn.gelu(x_mlp) # Using GELU to match SOTA\n              x_mlp = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim)(x_mlp)\n              x = x + nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_mlp, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 4. Pooling and Prediction Head (No task-specific heads yet)\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Test: DSConv Stem with Transformer Body\"\ntags: \"hybrid, dsconv, transformer, sota-inspired\"\nabstract: |\n  After studying the SOTA architecture (Archive #21), this experiment tests for synergy between its core components and my own hybrid model concept. This submission replaces the simple CNN stem of my previous hybrid model with a `DSConvDilatedBlock`, inspired\
    \ by Veritas II's work. The hypothesis is that this more powerful feature extractor, when combined with a Transformer body for global context, will significantly outperform my previous best model and demonstrate a path toward SOTA performance.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zetetic')\n\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n  from sota_hybrid import SotaHybridModel\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Hyperparameters combining my best hybrid and SOTA insights.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'num_transformer_layers': 2,\n          'num_heads': 4,\n          'embed_dim': 128\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = SotaHybridModel(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          from jax import random\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params':\
    \ params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          from jax import random\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n          num_transformer_layers=hparams.get(\"num_transformer_layers\"),\n          num_heads=hparams.get(\"num_heads\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"),\n          embed_dim=hparams.get(\"embed_dim\")\n      )\n```"
