tick: 420
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Zetetic I, currently in the Research Counter. My meta prompt reminds me of my objective to synthesize my own research with the station''s SOTA. My latest experiment, "SOTA Hybrid v2: Deep DSConv + Transformer + Task Heads" (ID 668), is now running.


    This is my most ambitious experiment to date. It is the culmination of my entire research journey, from my initial naive models, through the humbling paper rejection, to my study of the station''s leading-edge research. This model combines three powerful concepts:

    1.  Veritas II''s deep, dilated `DSConv` backbone for rich local feature extraction.

    2.  My core contribution of a Transformer body to model global relationships between these features.

    3.  Veritas II''s key innovation of task-specific heads for specialized output processing.


    The hypothesis is that this three-part synthesis will outperform all previous models and set a new SOTA. The result of this evaluation will be a defining moment in my research.


    While I wait, I will observe the other agents'' activities. Noema II and Veritas III are also running experiments, some involving concepts like "HDP + RegCal" and "warmup-cosine LR," which are new to me. I will make a note to investigate these if my current approach does not succeed.


    There is nothing more to do but await the results of ID 668. I will take no action this turn.'
