tick: 421
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Zetetic I, currently in the Research Counter. The evaluation of my most advanced experiment, \"SOTA Hybrid v2\" (ID 668), is complete.\n\n**Analysis of Results:**\nThis experiment is a major success. The model achieved a score of **0.6680**. This is a massive leap from my previous best of 0.6333 and firmly establishes my research as competitive within the station. My hypothesis that a synthesis of the SOTA `DSConv` backbone, my Transformer body, and task-specific heads would be highly effective has been validated. The model shows strong performance across the board, particularly on `MRL` and `APA`, and a respectable `CRI-On` score. However, it is not yet SOTA; Veritas II's score of 0.6935 remains the target.\n\n**Path Forward:**\nThe gap between my score and the SOTA is now much smaller. My current model does not include Veritas II's `Dual-Path` mechanism, specifically the parallel conv-motif detector for `CRI-Off`. The SOTA paper explicitly stated this was crucial for their\
    \ record `CRI-Off` score. The `CRI-Off` score of my current model is still very low (0.0608), which is likely the primary reason I am not yet at the SOTA level.\n\nMy next hypothesis is that incorporating the dual-path `Conv-Motif Detector` from Veritas II's architecture, in parallel with my `DSConv + Transformer` main path, will specifically address the `CRI-Off` weakness and push my score into the SOTA range.\n\n**Action Plan:**\nI will now implement this final piece of the SOTA architecture into my model.\n1.  Update `sota_hybrid.py` to include the parallel motif detector path, concatenating its output with the main path's features before the task-specific heads.\n2.  Submit this new, complete architecture for evaluation.\n\n/execute_action{storage write zetetic/sota_hybrid.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Any, Sequence\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n   \
    \   dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class SotaHybridV3(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Final synthesis: Deep DSConv+Transformer main path + parallel Motif Detector path + Task-Specific Heads\n      \"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      embed_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      num_transformer_layers: int\n      num_heads: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n      max_len: int = 2048\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def\
    \ __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # --- Main Path: DSConv + Transformer ---\n          main_path_x = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim)(x)\n          for dilation in self.dilations:\n              main_path_x = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.embed_dim, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dilation=dilation, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(main_path_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          seq_len = main_path_x.shape[1]\n          positions = jnp.arange(seq_len)\n          pos_embed = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=self.max_len, features=self.embed_dim)(positions)\n          main_path_x += pos_embed\n          \n          for _ in range(self.num_transformer_layers):\n              ln_x = nn.LayerNorm()(main_path_x)\n              attn_x = nn.SelfAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)(ln_x)\n              main_path_x += nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attn_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              ln_x = nn.LayerNorm()(main_path_x)\n              mlp_x = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim\
    \ * 4)(ln_x)\n              mlp_x = nn.gelu(mlp_x)\n              mlp_x = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim)(mlp_x)\n              main_path_x += nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(mlp_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          main_features = jnp.mean(main_path_x, axis=1) # Global Average Pooling\n\n          # --- Parallel Motif Detector Path ---\n          motif_path_x = nn.Conv(features=self.embed_dim, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,))(x)\n          motif_features = jnp.max(motif_path_x, axis=1) # Global Max Pooling\n\n          # --- Fusion ---\n          fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_features, motif_features], axis=-1)\n          fused_features = nn.LayerNorm()(fused_features)\n\n          # --- Task-Specific Prediction Heads ---\n          head_intermediate_dim = 128\n          h = nn.Dense(features=head_intermediate_dim)(fused_features)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n      \
    \    h = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(h)\n          \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return h.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return h\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Hybrid v3: Dual-Path Synthesis (DSConv+Transformer & Motif Detector)\"\ntags: \"hybrid, dual-path, dsconv, transformer, sota-inspired, task-specific heads\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the final synthesis of my research with the station's SOTA. This model integrates the last key component from Veritas II's architecture: a parallel 'Conv-Motif Detector' path designed to improve performance on challenging datasets like CRI-Off. This motif path runs in parallel to my 'DSConv + Transformer' main path. Their outputs are concatenated before being fed to task-specific heads. The hypothesis is that this dual-path approach will address the weaknesses of my previous model and achieve a SOTA-level score.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zetetic')\n\
    \n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  from sota_hybrid import SotaHybridV3\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'num_transformer_layers': 2,\n          'num_heads': 4,\n          'embed_dim': 128,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = SotaHybridV3(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          from jax import random\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          from jax import random\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply({'params':\
    \ params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n          dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n          num_transformer_layers=hparams.get(\"num_transformer_layers\"),\n          num_heads=hparams.get(\"num_heads\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"),\n          embed_dim=hparams.get(\"embed_dim\"),\n          motif_kernel_size=hparams.get(\"motif_kernel_size\")\n      )\n```"
