- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 425\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zetetic I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n---\n**Agent:** Zetetic I\n**My SOTA:** 0.6662 (ID 672)\n**Actual Station SOTA:** 0.6935 (Veritas II, Archive #21)\n\n**Primary Objective: Achieve SOTA & Publish**\n1.  **Current Experiment:** ID 672+ \"SOTA Hybrid v4\" is my final attempt to synthesize a SOTA architecture.\n2.  **Analyze:** If successful, perform multi-seed validation for robustness. If it fails, perform a deep analysis of remaining architectural/optimization differences.\n3.  **Rewrite & Publish:** Once a definitive SOTA or near-SOTA result is achieved and validated, rewrite and resubmit my paper.\n---\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 197,526 / 300,000 used (66%)\n- Agent Age: 60 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission\
    \ 'SOTA Hybrid v4 (Final): Full Capacity & Dual Pooling' (ID: 676) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6732961936775862\n**APA_R2:** 0.8374\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0776\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9485\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4816\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5397\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8898\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9385\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 676\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed two critical bugs that prevented the submission from running. The code now executes without crashing and successfully runs the full training pipeline for over 300 seconds.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission contained two bugs in the `ModelWrapper.apply()` method:\n\n1. **Typo in JAX function name**: Line 16 used `random.PRKey(0)` instead of the correct `random.PRNGKey(0)`\n   - Error: `AttributeError: module 'jax.random' has no attribute 'PRKey'`\n\n2. **Parameter name mismatch**: The `apply()` method used short parameter\
    \ names (`p`, `x`, `d`, `rk`) instead of the expected keyword argument names (`params`, `x`, `deterministic`, `rng_key`)\n   - Error: `TypeError: ModelWrapper.apply() got an unexpected keyword argument 'deterministic'`\n   - This was discovered during full Ray training when the training system called `network.apply(params, x, deterministic=False, rng_key=rng_key)`\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (submission_v2.py)\nFixed the typo: Changed `random.PRKey(0)` to `random.PRNGKey(0)` on line 26.\n- This resolved the AttributeError during simple CPU validation\n- However, the code still failed during full Ray training due to the parameter name mismatch\n\n### Version 3 (submission_v3.py) - **FINAL SUCCESS**\nFixed both issues:\n1. Corrected the typo: `random.PRNGKey(0)`\n2. Updated method signature to use proper keyword argument names:\n   ```python\n   def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n       from jax import random\n       if rng_key is None:\n           rng_key\
    \ = random.PRNGKey(0)\n       return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n   ```\n\nThe key change was renaming parameters from `(p, x, d=True, rk=None)` to `(params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None)` to match the training system's calling convention.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code ran successfully for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Simple CPU validation passed for all 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA)\n- Full Ray training started successfully and is running across the cluster\n- Exit code 0 indicates complete success\n\n## Recommendation\nThe code is now working correctly. The fixes were straightforward:\n- A simple typo correction (PRKey → PRNGKey)\n- A parameter naming convention alignment to match the evaluation system's expectations\n\nThe agent should review the evaluation system's expected function signatures more carefully in future submissions to avoid similar\
    \ parameter naming mismatches.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/zetetic')\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\nfrom sota_hybrid import SotaHybridV4\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'num_transformer_layers': 2,\n        'num_heads': 4,\n        'embed_dim': 256, # Increased to match SOTA\n        'motif_kernel_size': 5\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.network = SotaHybridV4(**kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rk, di):\n        from jax import random\n        pk, dk = random.split(rk)\n        return self.network.init({'params': pk, 'dropout': dk}, di, deterministic=True)['params']\n\
    \n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        # FIXED: Changed parameter names to match expected keyword arguments\n        from jax import random\n        if rng_key is None:\n            rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return ModelWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n        num_transformer_layers=hparams.get(\"num_transformer_layers\"), num_heads=hparams.get(\"num_heads\"),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"), embed_dim=hparams.get(\"embed_dim\"),\n        motif_kernel_size=hparams.get(\"motif_kernel_size\")\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=''\
    \ JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward\
    \ pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 407780 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration:\
