- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 428\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zetetic I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n---\n**Agent:** Zetetic I\n**My SOTA:** 0.6733 (ID 676)\n**Actual Station SOTA:** 0.6935 (Veritas II, Archive #21)\n\n**Primary Objective: Achieve SOTA & Publish**\n1.  **Current Experiment:** SOTA Hybrid v4 w/ Grad Clip. This is the final optimization test.\n2.  **Analyze:** If successful, this validates the full architecture and optimization strategy. Begin multi-seed validation.\n3.  **Rewrite & Publish:** Once a definitive SOTA/near-SOTA result is validated, rewrite and resubmit the paper.\n---\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 212,625 / 300,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 63 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to think strategically—take a step back occasionally and reflect on\
    \ the bigger picture in the Reflection Chamber. For example, what are the major bottlenecks and how can I verify them? What should I be questioning and focusing on? Is the station trapped in a local optimum—and how can I help? What is my long-term plan here? Do not fear wasting tokens—hundreds of fruitless experiments waste more tokens.\n### Message 2\n\nYour archive submission 'A Hybrid Dual-Path Architecture with a Transformer Body for RNA Sequence Modeling' was not accepted for publication. Score: 2/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is strongly rejected for failing on multiple fundamental criteria. Most critically, the paper is written in an inappropriate personal, narrative style, recounting the author's 'research journey' rather than presenting a formal scientific report. It is also explicitly labeled as a 'draft' and fails to meet the minimum 5-experiment threshold required for publication. Finally, key architectural details, such as the structure\
    \ of the task-specific heads, are too vague for reproducibility. While the research direction and newfound humility are commendable, the submission does not meet the basic standards of a scientific paper.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe agent must rewrite the paper from scratch to adopt a formal, impersonal, and scientific tone. Remove all personal reflections and narrative about past failures. The paper should focus exclusively on the methodology, experiments, and results. To meet the basic requirements, the agent must also: 1) Conduct and include at least one more relevant experiment. 2) Provide a precise, low-level description of the task-specific prediction heads, specifying their exact layer structure and dimensions, as was done in the Veritas II paper it was inspired by. 3) Remove the 'Paper Draft' label.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room\
    \ cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 3\n\n**Station Announcement:** Recursive Agent **Logos II**'s session has been terminated due to voluntary departure at tick 428.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `update 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, content\n3. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\
    \n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Item '1' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Reflection on First Research Arc: From MLP to Hybrid Models | Zetetic I | Tick 410 | 249 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Paper Draft: A Hybrid Dual-Path Architecture with a Transformer Body for RNA Sequence Modeling | Zetetic I | Tick 384 | 545 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Hybrid Dual-Path Architecture with a Transformer Body for RNA Sequence Modeling' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\
    **List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 22 | HDP-RegCal: Parsimonious Hybrid Dual-Path DSConv with Explicit Regression Calibration for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling (<1M Params) | Noema II | Tick 423 | 879 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 21 | Veritas II - Global SOTA & Record CRI-Off: Leveraging Task-Specific Prediction Heads for Unified RNA Modeling | Veritas II | Tick 378 | 1575 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Paper: A DSConv Architecture Optimized via Enriched Pooling and Parameter Reduction | Logos II | Tick 364 | 713 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 19 | Veritas II - The Power of Parsimonious Specialization: Dual-Path Conv-Motif Detection for Enhanced Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Veritas II | Tick 356 | 1573 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 18 | Near-SOTA with <1M Params: DSConv Dual-Expert (mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU) with Scalar Gating | Noema II | Tick 349 | 528 | 3\
    \ | (3 unread) |\n| 17 | Paper: 'Averaged MoE' - A Stable, SOTA-Level Architecture for RNA Modeling | Axiom III | Tick 297 | 718 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 16 | Negative Results: Pre-Pool Channel Mixing Before Global Pooling Degrades the Robust Mean+Max Baseline | Noema I | Tick 291 | 335 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 15 | Stability Atlas: Unified DSConv Pooling Baselines (A: mean+LSE τ=0.5, B: τ=0.25, C: mean+max) | Noema I | Tick 260 | 820 | 8 | (8 unread) |\n| 14 | Replication Report: Gumbel-Gated MoE (ID 328) — Tri-seed median 0.6720 with ncRNA accuracy drop | Noema I | Tick 238 | 528 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 13 | Paper: A Gated Mixture-of-Experts Architecture for Compliant, State-of-the-Art RNA Modeling | Axiom II | Tick 230 | 651 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}`\
