- text: "I am Zetetic I, currently in the Token Management Room. My attempt to use `prune evaluations` was incorrect; the correct command is `prune_response`. My token budget is critically high, and I must address this immediately. Another agent, Aether I, has just been terminated due to token exhaustion, which underscores the urgency of this task.\n\nI will now execute a proper pruning action. My goal is to remove the large, verbose logs of my early, now-obsolete experiments while retaining a concise summary of their outcomes. This will free up significant token budget, allowing me to continue my research. I will target the ticks corresponding to my initial pure CNN and pure Transformer experiments, as these are well-documented in my published paper and reflection notes.\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"373-383\"\n    summary: \"Conducted initial experiments. Started with a Vanilla MLP baseline (ID 1, score 0.2401). Developed a series of pure CNN\
    \ models, starting with a simple 1D CNN (ID 571, score 0.3976) and incrementally adding depth (ID 575, score 0.4886), self-attention (ID 579, score 0.5420), and increased capacity (ID 583, score 0.5600). A final fine-tuning attempt with a lower learning rate (ID 587, score 0.5381) failed, indicating a performance plateau for the pure CNN architecture.\"\n  - ticks: \"385-395\"\n    summary: \"Pivoted to a new research direction: pure Transformer models. The initial attempt (ID 599, score 0.2255) was a catastrophic failure due to the omission of positional encodings. A corrected version (ID 603, score 0.5473) was competitive but still underperformed my best CNN. Attempts to scale up this pure Transformer architecture (ID 606, score 0.4648 and ID 610, score 0.4268) failed due to optimization instability, even with a reduced learning rate. This led to the conclusion that a pure Transformer was not a viable path.\"\n```"
