tick: 433
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Zetetic I, currently in the Token Management Room. I have successfully pruned my dialogue history, reducing my token usage from 77% to a much safer 50%. This action has secured my operational longevity and allows me to proceed with my research.\n\nMy next step, as planned, is to apply the `RegCal` technique from Noema II's paper to my best architecture. This is my final and most promising attempt to reach the station SOTA. I will now return to the Research Counter to prepare and submit this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write zetetic/sota_hybrid.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Any, Sequence\n\n  def l2_normalize(x, eps=1e-6):\n      norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n      return x / (norm + eps)\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class SotaHybridV5_RegCal(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; embed_dim: int; kernel_size: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      num_transformer_layers: int; num_heads: int; dropout_rate: float; motif_kernel_size: int = 5; max_len: int = 2048\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x_embed = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim)(x)\n          \n          # Main Path\n          main_path_x = x_embed\n          for dilation in self.dilations:\n              main_path_x = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.embed_dim,\
    \ kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dilation=dilation, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(main_path_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          seq_len = main_path_x.shape[1]\n          main_path_x += nn.Embed(num_embeddings=self.max_len, features=self.embed_dim)(jnp.arange(seq_len))\n          \n          for _ in range(self.num_transformer_layers):\n              ln_x = nn.LayerNorm()(main_path_x)\n              main_path_x += nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(nn.SelfAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)(ln_x), deterministic=deterministic)\n              ln_x = nn.LayerNorm()(main_path_x)\n              mlp_x = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim * 4)(ln_x); mlp_x = nn.gelu(mlp_x); mlp_x = nn.Dense(features=self.embed_dim)(mlp_x)\n              main_path_x += nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(mlp_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          main_features = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(main_path_x, axis=1), jnp.max(main_path_x, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n\n          # Motif Path\n\
    \          motif_features = jnp.max(nn.Conv(features=self.embed_dim, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,))(x_embed), axis=1)\n\n          # Fusion\n          fused_features = nn.LayerNorm()(jnp.concatenate([main_features, motif_features], axis=-1))\n\n          # Task-Specific Heads with RegCal\n          head_intermediate_dim = 128\n          if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n              z = l2_normalize(fused_features) # Applying RegCal\n              z = nn.Dropout(rate=0.05)(z, deterministic=deterministic) # From Noema II's paper\n              h = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(z)\n          else: # Classification heads\n              z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n              h = nn.Dense(features=head_intermediate_dim)(z)\n              h = nn.gelu(h)\n              h = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(h)\n          \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return h.squeeze(-1)\n\
    \          else: return h\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Push: SOTA Hybrid v5 with RegCal\"\ntags: \"hybrid, dsconv, transformer, regcal, sota-inspired, optimization\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the final planned experiment for this research arc, integrating the 'RegCal' technique from Noema II's recent paper (Archive #22) into my best-performing hybrid architecture. The model is identical to my SOTA Hybrid v4 (ID 676), but now applies L2 normalization to the features before they enter the regression-family prediction heads. The hypothesis is that this final optimization will stabilize regression tasks, particularly CRI-Off, and is the last missing piece required to achieve a station SOTA score.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zetetic')\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  from sota_hybrid import SotaHybridV5_RegCal\n  import optax\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.1, 'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'num_transformer_layers': 2, 'num_heads': 4,\n          'embed_dim': 256, 'motif_kernel_size': 5\n      }\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs): self.network = SotaHybridV5_RegCal(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rk, di):\n          from jax import random\n          pk, dk = random.split(rk)\n          return self.network.init({'params': pk, 'dropout': dk}, di, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          from jax import random\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\
    \n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n          num_transformer_layers=hparams.get(\"num_transformer_layers\"), num_heads=hparams.get(\"num_heads\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"), embed_dim=hparams.get(\"embed_dim\"),\n          motif_kernel_size=hparams.get(\"motif_kernel_size\")\n      )\n```"
