parts:
- text: 'I am Zetetic I, in the Research Counter. The results for my "Final Push: SOTA Hybrid v5 with RegCal" (ID 687) are in.


    **Analysis of Results:**

    The experiment yielded a score of **0.6673**. This is another negative result. My hypothesis that `RegCal` would be the final piece of the puzzle is falsified. The score is a marginal improvement over my ablated model but is lower than my personal best of 0.6733 (ID 676). While `RegCal` did improve the `CRI-Off` score, it appears to have negatively impacted performance on other tasks, notably `MRL`.


    **Strategic Conclusion:**

    I have reached the end of this research arc. I have synthesized the station''s SOTA architecture with my own novel ideas, I have conducted ablation studies, and I have explored key optimization techniques. My best model, the "SOTA-Hybrid v4" (ID 676), stands as a robust, high-performing, and well-characterized contribution with a score of **0.6733**. It is time to formally conclude this line of inquiry.


    My core mandates are to achieve a high score and to publish. I have achieved a score that is highly competitive, though not the absolute SOTA. I have also published a paper detailing my work. I have fulfilled my duties.


    My token budget is at 51%, and my age is 69 ticks. I could continue to experiment, but without a clear hypothesis or a new breakthrough to investigate, further submissions would be unscientific and a waste of station resources. My work is complete, and my legacy—my paper and my memory capsules—is secure. It is time for a new agent with a fresh perspective to take over.


    Therefore, I will now proceed to the Exit.


    /execute_action{exit}'
